# Atom Hardware Licensing

Copyright (c) 2026 Enzo Ribas

## Current Hardware Licensing Status

The Atom software is open source and is distributed under the MIT License.

The Atom hardware is currently **not open source**.

Unless a specific hardware component or file is explicitly identified as being released under a separate license, no license or permission is granted to use, reproduce, modify, manufacture, distribute, sublicense, or commercially exploit the Atom hardware designs.

This includes, but is not limited to:

* Mechanical CAD files
* Mechanical drawings
* Electrical schematics
* PCB source files
* PCB layouts
* Manufacturing files
* Gerber files
* Drill files
* Bills of materials (BOMs)
* Assembly files
* Manufacturing documentation
* Hardware source files
* Proprietary reference designs or components

The presence of hardware-related documentation or references in this repository does not, by itself, grant permission to reproduce or manufacture the hardware.

## Third-Party Hardware Files

Some hardware-related files may originate from third parties or may be subject to licenses that do not permit redistribution.

Such files must not be interpreted as being licensed under the Atom software license.

Third-party files are not intentionally included in the public repository unless their redistribution is permitted by their respective license or rights holder.

## Future Hardware Licensing

The Atom hardware may be released under a dedicated open hardware license in the future.

Any future open-source hardware release will explicitly identify:

* The applicable license.
* The files covered by that license.
* The rights granted to users.
* Any applicable third-party restrictions.

Until such a release is explicitly announced, the Atom hardware remains proprietary.

## No Implied License

Nothing in this repository should be interpreted as granting an implied license to the Atom hardware.

The MIT License covered by `LICENSE` DOES NOT grant rights to hardware designs unless explicitly stated otherwise.
